{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Visits Vanessa in San Francisco"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Calling the Boss"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs in common social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear at work."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le04ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present vs. Present Continuous Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Present tense to talk about:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li>a routine action or specific action that happens regularly</li> <li>a general truth</li> <li>to give personal information</li> </ul> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use expressions of frequency like <span class=\"italic\">every day</span> or <span class=\"italic\">always</span> with the Present Simple."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You form the Present Continuous with the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be + verb-ing</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li>a current event or action happening around now</li> <li>events that <span class=\"strong\">are going to happen</span> soon (future plans)</li> </ul> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">right now</span> or <span class=\"italic\">later</span> with the Present Continuous."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I have three weeks of vacation left.</br></br>  Your benefit plan allows you to take 3 personal days during the year.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I am calling to ask for a few days off next days.</br></br>   I am hoping I can use some vacation time next week.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking for Clarification"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "If you don't understand what a person is saying, it is important to ask for clarification in a polite way.   </br></br>Here are some expressions you can use to ask for clarification."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li>Could you clarify what you mean by that?</li> <li>What do you mean by ... ?</li> <li>Do you mean ... ?</li> <li>Could you be more explicit about that?</li> <li>Could you give me an example?</li> </ul>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to earn"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to obtain after doing something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You must earn those days off. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "holiday"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "vacation; time you do not work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will have 3 weeks for a holiday at the end of your first year."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "benefit plan"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "extra advantages connected to a job, like health insurance"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your benefit plan includes personal days and health insurance."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "personal day"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a day you do not work, you do other things (but not vacation)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can take three personal days during the year. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "head chef"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person who is responsible for the kitchen in a restaurant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can use those days if your head chef agrees."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "manager"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who organizes the work of other people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm just a good manager."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "boss"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person who is in charge of a workplace"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Thank you Mr. Johnson! You're a great boss!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue of 7 - 9 lines. One person is the worker. The other person is the boss or manager."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask for time off."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use expressions asking for clarification."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice your dialogue with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write 9 lines about a boss and a worker."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask for clarification in a dialogue."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice speaking with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I change roles in a dialogue."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le04ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le04ob06re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le04ob06re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Johnson</span>: Hello?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Hello?  Mr. Johnson?<br /><span class =\"strong\">Mr. Johnson</span>: Hello Vanessa. How are you?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  I'm fine, Mr. Johnson. A friend of mine is visiting from Cambridge. I'm calling to ask for a few days off in the next few days. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Johnson</span>: What do you mean by days off?", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le04ob06re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'm hoping I can use some vacation time next week.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Johnson</span>: Well, Vanessa, you just started in your new position as sous-chef a few weeks ago.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes, Mr. Johnson, but I have three weeks of vacation left.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Johnson</span>: You must earn those days off, Vanessa. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Could you be more explicit?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Johnson</span>: Well, you will have 3 weeks holiday at the end of your first year.", "id": 2, "time": "14500", "image": "engenn5le04ob06re2img10.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh, I didn't realize that. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Johnson</span>: Yes, but your benefit plan allows you to take 3 personal days during the year.  You can use those days if your head chef agrees.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh, thank you Mr. Johnson!  You're a great boss!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Johnson</span>:  